[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3392285050","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111489#issuecomment-3392285050","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111489","id":3392285050,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KMil6","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-10T20:54:12Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T20:54:33Z","body":"- Related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111457.\n\nSee discussion about the Normalized property that was added to AreaLight3D in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108219.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3392285050/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3392329011","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111489#issuecomment-3392329011","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111489","id":3392329011,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KMtUz","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-10T21:16:00Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T21:16:00Z","body":"Ya, in general normalizing the brightness is way more intuitive for most users. This was an intentional choice. It really sucks for users that tweaking the size to get slightly softer shadows and a slightly softer specular highlight results in their entire scene brightness changing. Its the same with spotlights where changing the cone angle doesn't change the intensity.\n\nAlso, in Blender this behaviour is the default https://docs.blender.org/manual/en/latest/render/lights/light_object.html. To get the behaviour you describe, you have to turn the \"normalize\" setting off\n\nBoth the [Filament docs](https://google.github.io/filament/Filament.md.html#lighting/directlighting) and the Frostbite PBR paper have good discussions about this https://seblagarde.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/07/course_notes_moving_frostbite_to_pbr_v32.pdf ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3392329011/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3392694150","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111489#issuecomment-3392694150","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111489","id":3392694150,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KOGeG","user":{"login":"betalars","id":18014034,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDE0MDM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18014034?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars","html_url":"https://github.com/betalars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-11T00:57:49Z","updated_at":"2025-10-11T00:57:49Z","body":"> To get the behaviour you describe, you have to turn the \"normalize\" setting off\n\nno, that is not what my report is about.\n\nLet me visualize that for you. Left to right are different light sources top and bottom are diffuse and specular.\n\nleft is a small light source.\nnext to it is a light source scaled up and normalized\nthe most left light source is scaling up without normalizing.\nthe purple one third from left is the current godot implementation where only specular gets brighter and not the diffuse. This is just objectively wrong no matter how you put it.\n\n<img width=\"2114\" height=\"1083\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4917f179-1f23-43e7-bcaf-0116678747e1\" />\n\nThere can be a discussion if you want to scale up the intensity when you make the light softer. I would argue that is not intuitive.\n\nBut only making the specular highlight brighter the larger the light gets is objectively wrong.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3392694150/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3405730271","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111489#issuecomment-3405730271","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111489","id":3405730271,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7K_1Hf","user":{"login":"betalars","id":18014034,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDE0MDM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18014034?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars","html_url":"https://github.com/betalars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T10:30:38Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T10:30:38Z","body":"I think if it wasn't clear enough, this godot versus blender comparison should help. The light sources have a comparible diffuse brightness and are visualised trough a mesh via a translucent/backlight shader. You can compare the brightness of the diffuse component versus the brightness of the reflection.\n\n<img width=\"576\" height=\"1050\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8009f7c0-a7f1-420a-89a9-3b161e5128f9\" />\n\n<img width=\"462\" height=\"868\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1935df87-538b-42da-b3b7-fb901e5eae5e\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3405730271/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3407580665","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111489#issuecomment-3407580665","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111489","id":3407580665,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LG435","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T17:40:12Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T17:40:12Z","body":"You are comparing apples and oranges. The blender render is a direct reflection of an object while the Godot reflection is a specular reflection from a light source. If you want to recreate that bottom shot in Godot you need to add something to do reflections like a reflection probe or Screen Space Reflections","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3407580665/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3411456099","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111489#issuecomment-3411456099","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111489","id":3411456099,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LVrBj","user":{"login":"betalars","id":18014034,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDE0MDM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18014034?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars","html_url":"https://github.com/betalars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T15:27:45Z","updated_at":"2025-10-16T15:27:45Z","body":"> You are comparing apples and oranges.\n\nI am sorry that I confused you by using a rendering made in cycles in addition to the other comparison rendering I used in the initial description of the issue.\n\nHowever while trying to make myself more clear, I did make a new observation. This issue seems to relate to the interaction of low roughness and big light sources.\n\nThis is a comparison of 3 lights with identical energy, two of them being reflected on a plane with roughness of 0.33, and the last one being reflected by a plane with roughness of 0.1. I would say there is some issue with the conversation of energy.\n\n<img width=\"1417\" height=\"722\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/70f615d2-4c3e-493e-ae0a-461cfb1f1481\" />\n\nBlender eevee on the other hand does not seem to have this issue.\n\n<img width=\"1369\" height=\"749\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/576bd69b-cd4c-43e3-9389-b4a5d612c4bc\" />\n\nI will also say that the rough surfaces in eevee do look a lot more rough and smooth and I have noticed how materials with large roughness in godot look kind of kind of ... harsh.\n\n<img width=\"1369\" height=\"749\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/31b28a56-3db0-43ff-924d-33de2f5950b6\" />\n\nI will also note how eeve does produce strikingly similar results to cycles and therefore I do not think this is an issue that has much to do with rasterization versus ray tracing. No I am not using eevee ray tracing to mess with my results and I have disabled the flossy reflections for the spheres that are only visible to the camera so the setup is more intuitive to understand.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3411456099/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3411563211","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111489#issuecomment-3411563211","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111489","id":3411563211,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LWFLL","user":{"login":"betalars","id":18014034,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDE0MDM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18014034?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars","html_url":"https://github.com/betalars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T15:55:57Z","updated_at":"2025-10-16T16:01:27Z","body":"To help clear up things, have a comparison of blender eevee specular highlights versus godot specular highlights without thew spheres.\n\nComparing diffuse brightness against specular reflections.\n\n<img width=\"1441\" height=\"750\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/551c6432-8503-4878-a190-1698db3dd2d4\" />\n\n<img width=\"1441\" height=\"750\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa152d6c-0f6b-455d-93fb-a62244238b4e\" />\n\nGodot has pretty much the exact setup in terms of materials. I am also using the default light settings of godot. I a am using normalized brightness for blender because you said that was the intended implementation for godot.\n\nI think there is a lot of to unpack here.\n\nFirst of all I cannot reproduce your claim that light sources in godot do get brighter when they get bigger. The diffuse highlight for each 3 lamps is exactly the same for each size in godot. When I switch off the normalized lighting option in blender, the diffuse highlight gets brighter.\n\nAlso the energy of the reflection clearly stays consistent in blender regardless of the roughness where in godot it is frankly all over the place.\n\nIf you think this is expected behavior and not a bug, I don't think I can contribute much more to this discussion.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3411563211/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3412141347","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111489#issuecomment-3412141347","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111489","id":3412141347,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LYSUj","user":{"login":"betalars","id":18014034,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDE0MDM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18014034?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars","html_url":"https://github.com/betalars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/betalars/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T18:00:34Z","updated_at":"2025-10-16T18:00:34Z","body":"I can't anymore.\n\nIf this is not a bug, then let's have a [discussion](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/13407)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3412141347/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]